# Chord Melody: First Ballad (repertoire plan: st-chord-melody-1). An original 16-bar ballad in
# C major for solo guitar. The melody is always on strings 1 and 2 and always the highest note;
# on beats 1 and 3 a chord sits under it (C, Am, F, G7, Em and Dm), between them the melody moves
# alone. Form: phrase 1 (bars 1-4, ending on G7), phrase 2 (5-8, home to C), a bridge (9-12,
# through Em and Dm) and a last phrase (13-16, home to C).
# The chords are the open shapes with the melody note on top. For the A on top of Am (bars 2, 6
# and 14) the hand moves up to fifth position (finger 1 across strings 1 to 3 at fret 5, finger 3
# on string 4 fret 7) and comes back down after the long note. Each chord symbol shows the grip
# played under it.
title: Chord Melody: First Ballad
composer: Sixstring Academy
source: Original chord-melody ballad
licence: Original study for Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 6
tags: chord melody, fingerstyle, ballad, solo
tempo: 66
time: 4/4
key: C

